extraction_notes: "Lone Star printed 41-43 (cache p042-p044, page = folio + 1), read off 170 dpi renders. The entry points to the Dog Boy R.C.C. (printed 32-36) for special powers, psionics, equipment, money and I.C.; those are restated here from printed 33-36, so the class is self-contained and pairs with no race. Section heading: the Dog Pack R.C.C. chapter, a race, so men_of_arms: false. || XP: the ladder headed Dog Boy: K-9 Sniffer on the unnumbered page after printed 174 (cache p176), lower bounds. || ATTRIBUTES as printed 41: I.Q. 3D6+2, M.E. 3D6, M.A. 3D6, P.S. 3D6, P.P. 3D6, P.E. 3D6+4, P.B. 3D6, Spd 3D6 running, 1D6 digging (a natural ability). The entry says its bonuses are in addition to the Dog Boy''s Physical Bonuses (printed 33): +1D4 P.E., 1D4 P.S., +2D6 Spd, stored in bonuses.attributes. I.Q. 10 or higher is the R.C.C. requirement, stored as attribute_requirements and as a restriction line. || POOLS: S.D.C. 22 plus those gained from physical skills is a racial pool, stored as bonuses.pools.sdc 22, not sdc_base. Hit points P.E. plus 1D6 per level. P.P.E. 4D6 (the Sniffer''s own line; the Dog Boy prints 3D6). || BONUSES from printed 33: +2 initiative, +1 strike, parry and dodge, +2 save vs disease, +2 vs possession, and +1 to save vs psionic attack and all forms of mind control (psionics 1, mind_control 1). The 10-or-higher master psionic save is text in the Psionics ability. || PSIONICS: the Sniffer says see the Dog Boy; printed 33 gives Sense Evil, Sense Magic, Sixth Sense, Empathy and one more Sensitive power, considered a master psionic, I.S.P. M.E. plus 1D6x10, +10 per additional level. The Recognize Psychic Scent line prints ''10% 44% per additional level''; read as 10% +4%. || TRACKING BONUS +6% to the breed''s olfactory identification and tracking skills: written into the Superior Sense of Smell text beside the Dog Boy''s printed bases (70, 54 and 40 become 76, 60 and 46). || SPECIALIZED SCENT TRAINING: pick two of five, stored as a choose-2 ability group with each area''s base skill, penalties and range as text. The untrained-dog notes under each area describe other dogs and are not stored. || SKILLS (printed 43): American (the catalog row Language: Native Tongue) and Spanish at 90%, per_level 0. Basic Math 45+15 = 60. Radio: Basic 45+10 = 55. Read Sensory Equipment is Sensory Equipment 30+10 = 40. Track (by sight/skill; +15%) is Tracking (people) 25+15 = 40. Intelligence 32+10 = 42. Pilot Motorcycle/Hovercycle (+5%) is one printed line; stored as a choice of one of the two catalog skills at +5% (judgement: the slash read as either). Climbing and Running carry no bonus. Land Navigation 36+20 = 56. Wilderness Survival 30+15 = 45. W.P. Energy Pistol, W.P. Energy Rifle, one W.P. of choice. Hand to Hand: Expert, to Martial Arts for one other skill; no other style is offered. || RELATED: five, plus one at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12. Communications +5, Domestic +10, Electrical Basic Electronics only, Espionage any except Sniper, Mechanical Basic Mechanics and Automotive only, Medical ''None, other than the R.C.C. skill'' (the Sniffer''s R.C.C. list has no medical skill, so none), Military +10, Physical except Acrobatics and Boxing, Pilot sail and motor boats, motorcycle, hovercycle, jet pack and truck +5, Pilot Related any, Rogue none, Science any except chemistry (stored as the one skill named Chemistry), Technical +5 except computer operation and programming, W.P. any, Wilderness +5. Secondary: six at level one and two more at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12, same list without the bonuses. The never-taught-to-read note is a restriction line and excludes nothing, because a feral or Free Born dog is outside it. || EQUIPMENT: ''basically the same as the Dog Boy R.C.C.'', restated from printed 36. Light or heavy Dog Pack DPM riot armor is the one row dog-pack-dpm-riot-armor. PDD pocket audio recorder is pdd-pocket-audio-digital-disc-recorder-player. 100 ft of lightweight rope is lightweight-rope x1. A pair of vibro-knives or vibro-claws is a choice at qty 2; the vibro-saber or neuro-mace many also have is in the note, not granted. C-14 Fire Breather or CP-40, four additional E-clips. Telescopic sight and nightvision scope are in the rifle''s note. || MONEY: ''same as the Dog Boy R.C.C.'': 200-300 credits a month and player characters start with two months pay, a range of 400-600. Stored as 600, the figure the held dog-boy class carries; the range and the provided housing are in a restriction line. || Typical missions, tours of duty and maximum rank are printed for the Dog Boy soldier only and are not restated."
---

## Lore

Among the Coalition''s mutant dogs, a few are picked out for the quality of their
nose, their stamina and their wits, and sent for scent schooling at the
training grounds raised over an old pre-Rifts air base, at the Lone Star
Complex or at Chi-Town. They come out as K-9 Agents, called Sniffers.

A Sniffer still hunts psychics, mages and the supernatural like any Dog Boy,
but its trade is the scents nobody else can read: explosives, narcotics,
hidden bionics, illness in a living body, the weather before it turns. Most
come from the hound breeds and the shepherds. They are patient, cooperative
pack workers and very hard to shake once they have a trail.

## GM Notes

The class restates the Dog Boy''s sensing abilities and physical bonuses so it
stands alone; do not pair it with the Mutant Dog race. The two scent
specialties are chosen at creation. The breed and size tables are not rolled
for a Sniffer, and the mutation table is the G.M.''s call. A Sniffer outside
Coalition service is a deserter or Free Born and is hunted as one.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'k-9-sniffer');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'k-9-sniffer';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-k-9-sniffer-class.sql');
